{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Wade in the water, children,
[Am]Wade in the water, [Em]children,
[Em]Wade in the water, children,
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[Em]See that band all dressed in red,
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water;
[Am]Looks like the band that [Em]Moses led,
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[Em]Look over yonder, what do you see?
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water;
The [Am]Holy Ghost a-[Em]coming on me,
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
[Em]If you don't believe I've been redeemed,
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water;
Just [Am]follow me down to [Em]Jordan's stream,
God's a-[D]going to trouble the [Em]water.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: Em}
